&lt;p&gt;SWAPI (The Star Wars API) is one of the most popular free APIs for learning REST APIs in React, Vue, or vanilla JS — but it only returns JSON text. There are no images for Luke Skywalker, Tatooine, or the Millennium Falcon.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Furthermore, the old image host frequently used in tutorials (starwars-visualguide.com) currently has broken SSL certificates, failing to load across modern browsers.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;To solve this, I created a free static image API where every image matches the exact same ID used by SWAPI:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://starwarsgallery.netlify.app/assets/%7Bcategory%7D/%7Bid%7D.jpg" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://starwarsgallery.netlify.app/assets/{category}/{id}.jpg&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It covers 238 images across 5 categories: people, planets, species, starships, and vehicles.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


How to Use It (JavaScript)
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;
javascript
const getSwapiImage = (category, swapiUrl) =&amp;gt; {
const id = swapiUrl.split('/').filter(Boolean).pop();
return `https://starwarsgallery.netlify.app/assets/${category}/${id}.jpg`;
};

// Fetch data from SWAPI
const res = await fetch('https://swapi.dev/api/people/1/');
const luke = await res.json();

// Get the matching image
const imageUrl = getSwapiImage('people', luke.url);
console.log(imageUrl); 
// Output: "https://starwarsgallery.netlify.app/assets/people/1.jpg"
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F3tm1g6vyrw1xd0ogs160.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F3tm1g6vyrw1xd0ogs160.png" alt=" " width="800" height="595"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

